# What does not belong in the repository.
#
# Two things here differ from the usual Python .gitignore, and both matter:
#
#   * The .spec files are SOURCE. The standard template ignores *.spec because
#     PyInstaller usually generates them; ours are hand-written, name what goes
#     into each build and what is left out, and "Build EXE.bat" will not run
#     without them. They are listed as kept at the bottom of this file.
#   * The release zips are around 112 MB each. GitHub refuses any file over
#     100 MB, so leaving them out is what lets a push succeed at all. Put built
#     programs on a Releases page instead of in the tree.

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# PyInstaller's working folder and the finished programs: ~170 MB, rebuilt from
# source at any time by "Build EXE.bat".
build/
dist/

# --- Releases -------------------------------------------------------------
# The packaged folders and zips handed to viewers. Too big for the tree, and
# regenerated for every version.
EasyAI - V*/
EasyAI - V*.zip
*.7z

# --- The user's own things ------------------------------------------------
# settings.json holds absolute paths to this machine's ComfyUI, the remembered
# seeds and the chosen models. Committing it would point everyone else's copy
# at folders that do not exist for them.
settings.json
easyai-setup.json
# EasyAI Setup's editable install list, written beside Setup on first run.
# The real list is setup/catalog.json; this is a per-machine copy of it.
setup-settings.json
setup-settings.old.json
# The model lists ComfyUI last offered, so the Model and LoRA dropdowns work
# while it is closed. Rewritten every time EasyAI reads the engine.
engine-models.json

# Everything made with EasyAI: pictures, videos and enhanced prompts. Large,
# personal, and none of it is source.
output/

# The workflows exactly as exported from ComfyUI, before they were cleaned up
# for shipping (personal LoRA, sample boxes and the author's own pictures).
workflow-originals/

# --- Downloads and staging ------------------------------------------------
# Gated models copied here before being uploaded to the mirror - tens of GB.
mirror-staging/
# A part-finished download from EasyAI Setup.
*.part

# --- Windows --------------------------------------------------------------
# Shortcuts embed the absolute path of the machine that made them, so they are
# useless to anyone else. The .bat launchers beside them are the portable
# version and ARE committed.
*.lnk
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Credentials ----------------------------------------------------------
# EasyAI Setup asks for the HuggingFace and Civitai keys each run and never
# writes them down, so there is no key file to lose. These are here so that
# stays true if that ever changes.
.env
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json

# --- Scratch --------------------------------------------------------------
# Left behind by shell redirects while working on the build; safe to delete.
se.txt
so.txt
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
dist-trim/
build-trim/

# --- Claude Code project files ---------------------------------------------
# Local tooling config (agents, commands, settings) - not part of the app.
.claude/

# --- Kept on purpose ------------------------------------------------------
# Listed explicitly so a later edit, or a generic template pasted over this
# file, cannot quietly drop them.
!EasyAI.spec
!EasyAI Setup.spec
!EasyAI Studio.spec
!build_common.py
!workflows/**/*.json
!lang/*.json
!setup/catalog.json
!setup/mirror_links.json
!setup/url_overrides.json
